From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:24:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: CSSOM serialization as in Chrome: numbers keep six
 significant digits, lighting-color is a property, @keyframes and @supports
 rule text, @page margin descriptors serialize as one margin, family names as
 identifiers only when they are one plain identifier

- serialize_a_number (C++ and Rust): 1.23456789 is 1.23457 and 100 / 3 is 33.3333, as in Chrome; below 1 and from 10^6 up the six-decimal rule is unchanged
- lighting-color (Filter Effects 1): a non-inherited <color>, initial white
- @keyframes: each keyframe on its own line, two-space indent; @supports with no rules is ' {\n}'
- @page / margin-rule descriptors expanded from margin keep their longhand names, and the four sides serialize as one margin shorthand in shortest form (was 'margin: 1cm' four times)
- font-family: "Arial" serializes as Arial, Times New Roman as "Times New Roman"
- Painting/PaintFacts.cpp: GC::Weak::ptr() returns a GC::Ptr, so the in-process compositor context lookups take .ptr().ptr() (the series did not build at this file)
